# Copy to the private env file and fill it in; never commit real keys:
#   mkdir -p -m 700 ~/.config/companion-hackathon && cp .env.example ~/.config/companion-hackathon/.env && chmod 600 ~/.config/companion-hackathon/.env
# Plain NAME=value lines: no `export`, no spaces around =; one pair of surrounding quotes is dropped.
# Each user brings their own keys (decision 0003). Each program reads only the names it uses (Andy, the voice server
# and the offline eyes each their own list); nothing else in the file is passed on.

# Nebius Token Factory: the conversation, the eyes, hard questions, the scam check.
NEBIUS_API_KEY=
NEBIUS_BASE_URL=https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1/
# Tavily: the web. Its requests carry X-Project-ID (default "andy-companion").
TAVILY_API_KEY=
# TAVILY_PROJECT=andy-companion

# The eyes: token-factory (the default, Nemotron 3.5 Super VL), endpoint (our own, below), local (Cosmos, below) or off.
# ANDY_VISION=token-factory
# ANDY_VISION_MODEL=nvidia/Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL
# With ANDY_VISION=endpoint, the address and token cloud/vision-endpoint.sh prints:
# ANDY_VISION_URL=
# ANDY_VISION_TOKEN=
# Offline eyes (decision 0015): NVIDIA Cosmos Reason 2 2B on this computer (local-eyes/run.sh). Used when the eyes
# above can't be reached; ANDY_VISION=local uses it always. GPU 0 unless ANDY_LOCAL_EYES_GPU says otherwise.
# ANDY_VISION_FALLBACK=local
# ANDY_LOCAL_EYES_GPU=0
# The 2B model by default; with a whole 24 GB GPU free, the 8B one finds more precisely (decision 0015):
# ANDY_LOCAL_EYES_MODEL=nvidia/Cosmos-Reason2-8B
# ANDY_LOCAL_EYES_MEMORY=0.92
# ANDY_LOCAL_EYES_CONTEXT=12288
# Its port (default 8095); if you change it, give Andy the matching address too:
# ANDY_LOCAL_EYES_PORT=8095
# ANDY_LOCAL_EYES_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8095/v1
# The second look (Nemotron 3.5 Content Safety), from cloud/guard-endpoint.sh; without it Andy runs on the word list:
# ANDY_GUARD_URL=
# ANDY_GUARD_TOKEN=

# Nebius AI Cloud: the job scripts in cloud/ read only NEBIUS_API_KEY from this file. Set the project in your shell
# instead (export NEBIUS_JOB_PROJECT=..., a project whose region allows CPU VMs for jobs); without it they use the
# Nebius CLI's configured project, as the endpoint scripts always do.

# Optional: the GPU for the voice server (default 0), and the screen server's port (default 8090).
# ANDY_VOICE_GPU=1
# The voice server's model (default nvidia/Nemotron-3_5-Lightning), its longest turn in seconds (default 40; 0 turns
# the cap off), and the address Andy reaches it at:
# ANDY_MODEL=nvidia/Nemotron-3_5-Lightning
# ANDY_MAX_TURN_S=40
# ANDY_VOICE_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8765/v1/realtime
# ANDY_SCREEN_PORT=8090
# The finder turns its body to look past the head's 60 degrees (decision 0016); off keeps the head's reach.
# ANDY_FINDER_TURN=on

# Optional display-only object outline from a separately run, licensed local mask service (docs/object-outline.md).
# Disabled by default. Numeric loopback HTTP only; use a port DIFFERENT from the screen/voice servers.
# ANDY_OUTLINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8096

# Testing only. Keeps every finder try and every "what do you see?" look (pictures of the room, and what the eyes
# said; never the person's words) in this folder, to score or to see why something wasn't recognised.
# Leave it unset at any other time, and always while filming: the pictures show the room and whoever is in it.
# ANDY_FINDER_RECORD=
